            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 11 changed paths. The fsstore change opens with O_NONBLOCK on unix and then requires the opened file to be regular and the same file as the one looked at, which closes the FIFO hang and inode-reuse window; it tightens behavior and introduces no new exposure.",
              "engine/review/names.go fixes isLowerHex precedence so only 0-9 and a-f pass. The base condition accepted other characters (for example g-z), so this narrows validation and is a security improvement.",
              "engine/reviewverdict/decide.go changes are renames of the fate constants plus comment updates, and engine/review/handoff.go introduces the FileRef struct, so call sites keep the same argument order semantics. Decide logic is unchanged, and no secrets, authorization, or dependency changes are present."
            ]
          }
        }
